FIRE COUNTRY PATROL LOG — ACTIVE
Konohagakure Border Watch

Patrol Sector: Western forest belt, Land of Fire
Team: Two-genin patrol under a chunin lead

Log:
- Day 1: Departed the village gate at dawn. Cleared the western ridge
  waypoints; no activity. Refreshed the boundary trap markers.
- Day 2: Encountered a lost civilian herbalist; escorted to the road.
  Faint unfamiliar chakra signature noted near the river ford, unresolved
  — flagged to the sensor corps.
- Day 3: Uneventful. Standard checkpoints clear. Wildlife only.

Assessment: Sector nominal. The river-ford signature warrants a sensor
follow-up but showed no hostile behavior. No sign of Akatsuki or Sound
activity in this sector.

Next patrol to re-check the river ford. Log continued on return.
Filed by patrol lead.
